---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// The same policy as content/legal/privacy-policy.md in the game's repo; change both together.
const email = 'support@nutrx-labs.com';

const short = [
  { title: 'Nothing collected', text: 'No names, photos, locations, contacts or usage data. Nothing leaves the device.' },
  { title: 'No ads, no tracking', text: 'No advertising and no analytics or tracking tools of any kind.' },
  { title: 'No accounts', text: 'Nobody signs up or logs in.' },
  { title: 'Stays on the device', text: 'Game progress and settings live only on your iPhone or iPad.' },
];
---

<Base page="privacy" title="Where's My Crown? – Privacy Policy" description="How Where's My Crown? handles your family's information: it collects nothing.">
  <section class="night">
    <div class="container narrow hero">
      <h1 class="title">PRIVACY POLICY</h1>
      <p>Effective date: 23 October 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="short-h">
    <div class="container narrow short">
      <h2 id="short-h" class="pixel">The short version</h2>
      <div class="cards">
        {short.map((s) => (
          <div class="card">
            <p class="ui">{s.title}</p>
            <p>{s.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="container narrow policy">
    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Where's My Crown? ("the app") is a maze game for young children made by Nutrx Labs ("we", "us"). You can
        reach us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing. The app has no accounts, no sign-in, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking, and it contains no
        third-party code that collects data. We never see who plays it, how they play or where they are.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">What the app keeps on your device</h2>
      <p>To remember where your child got to, the app saves a few things on the device itself. They are never sent to us or anyone else:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>which mazes are open, and the stars earned in each;</li>
        <li>dress-up choices (dress and hair colours, and whether the little sister comes along);</li>
        <li>the Sound and Read aloud settings from the grown-ups' area;</li>
        <li>the day the free unicorn was last used (without the Royal Pass, the unicorn comes along once a day).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Deleting the app deletes all of this. <strong>Reset maze progress</strong> in the grown-ups' area clears the
        mazes and stars.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        The Royal Pass is a one-time in-app purchase made through Apple's App Store. Apple handles the payment and
        your Apple Account; we never see your name, payment card or any other personal information. The app doesn't
        keep its own record of the purchase: it asks Apple, on the device, whether the pass is owned, so it can unlock
        the helpers. Purchases sit behind a grown-up question so children can't buy by accident. Apple's
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">privacy policy</a> covers the purchase itself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Advertising</h2>
      <p>The app contains no advertising of any kind.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Read aloud and permissions</h2>
      <p>
        The voice that reads messages aloud is recorded audio built into the app. The app doesn't use the microphone,
        camera, location, contacts or photos, and doesn't send notifications. Nothing your child says or does is
        recorded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The app is made for children of about 3 to 6 and is listed in the App Store's Kids Category. We don't
        knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children, in line with the Children's Online
        Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and the GDPR's rules for children. The app has no chat, sharing or social
        features. Everything meant for grown-ups (the settings, the Royal Pass and the link to this page) sits behind
        a parental gate, and the child's side of the game never shows a price, a store or a link out of the app. If
        you believe a child has sent us personal information (for example by email), contact us and we will delete
        it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">If you email us</h2>
      <p>
        If you write to us for support, we use your email address and message only to answer you. We delete support
        emails within 12 months, or sooner if you ask.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">This website</h2>
      <p>
        This website uses no cookies, analytics or third-party requests: its fonts and pictures are served from the
        site itself. It's hosted on GitHub Pages, which may keep standard server logs (such as IP addresses) for
        security, under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to ask what information we hold about you, to correct it or
        to have it deleted. Because the app doesn't collect personal information, the only information we might hold
        is a support email you sent us. Write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> and we'll help.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="ui">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change how the app handles information, we'll update this page and the effective date at the top before
        the change takes effect. If a change would mean collecting any personal information from children, we would
        ask for a parent's permission first, as the law requires.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p>Questions? See <a href="/support">Support</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 64px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(22px, 3.6vw, 36px); line-height: 1.35; }
  .hero p { font-size: 18px; color: var(--on-night-2); }


  .short {
    padding-top: 40px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .short h2 { font-size: clamp(16px, 2.2vw, 22px); line-height: 1.5; }
  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(240px, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .card {
    background: var(--card);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--ink);
    padding: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .card .ui { font-size: 22px; line-height: normal; }

  .policy {
    padding-top: 48px;
    padding-bottom: 80px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 36px;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .policy section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .policy h2 { font-size: 28px; }
  .policy ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
</style>
